From: Abbas Rizvi <abbas.rizvi@nomadrail.com>
Subject: [TRIAG-8585] vdsrail.py — Bugs 1, 2a, 2b, 7 (firmware regex, SNMP-None
 guards, reboot hostname guard)

File: lib/device/vendor/vdsrail.py

Bug 1  firmware-version regex must also match "default image is now"
Bug 2a firmware polling loop must skip None SNMP results
Bug 2b config   polling loop must skip None SNMP results
Bug 7  reboot() must not SNMP-set hostname when the SNMP-get returned None

NOTE on Bug 7 context: the field carries two patcher generations. The current
one (scripts/fix_obn_bugs67.py) assumes the pre-patch line is

    hostname = self._snmp_get(...["snmp_get_hostname_oid"]) or ""

If your tree instead has it without the `or ""` suffix, use hunk @@7-alt@@
(commented at the bottom of this file) instead of hunk @@7@@.
---
--- a/lib/device/vendor/vdsrail.py
+++ b/lib/device/vendor/vdsrail.py
@@ Bug 1: set_firmware_version() regex @@
-        matchstr = r"Not running. System Firmware image loaded \[(.*)\]"
+        # Handle both response formats depending on switch firmware state
+        matchstr = r"Not running. System Firmware (?:default image is now|image loaded \[)(.*?)\]?"
@@ Bug 2a: firmware-task polling loop None guard @@
         result = ""
         for _ in range(120):
             sleep(1)
             result = self._snmp_get(
                 self.device_config["snmp_firmware_task_running_oid"]
             )
+            if not result:
+                continue
             search = re.search("Not running", result)
@@ Bug 2b: config-task polling loop None guard @@
         for _ in range(120):
             sleep(1)
             result = self._snmp_get(self.device_config["snmp_config_task_running_oid"])
+            if not result:
+                continue
             search = re.search("Not running", result)
@@ Bug 7: reboot() hostname None guard @@
     def reboot(self) -> bool:
-        hostname = self._snmp_get(self.device_config["snmp_get_hostname_oid"]) or ""
-        self._snmp_set({self.device_config["snmp_set_hostname_oid"]: hostname})
+        hostname = self._snmp_get(self.device_config["snmp_get_hostname_oid"])
+        if hostname is not None:
+            self._snmp_set({self.device_config["snmp_set_hostname_oid"]: hostname})
         self._snmp_set({self.device_config["snmp_reboot_oid"]: 3})

